  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following positive sentiment spikes (e.g., sentiment > 0.00) by 5-15% to avoid overreaction.",
    "Adjust downward for persistent negative sentiment (sentiment < 0.00) by applying a 3-7% bias correction to prevent underestimation.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast deviates > 10% from recent 5-day average, adjust toward historical mean.",
    "Correct for lagged overestimation: if true outcome is 2-3 days below forecast, reduce next forecast by 2-5% to account for delayed correction.",
    "When sentiment is neutral (0.00) and forecast is consistently above true outcome, apply a 5-10% downward bias to reflect market equilibrium.",
    "For high volatility periods (e.g., 3+ consecutive days with sentiment ±0.20), reduce forecast variance by 10-20% to avoid overfitting."
  ]
